# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — CLIF hospice pipeline
# =============================================================================

# ---- data: never commit patient-level or site data --------------------------
# site intermediates that may contain identifiers
*_private_data/
# generated shareable aggregates (regenerated by a run)
*_upload_to_box/
# generated federated aggregates
federated_outputs/
data/
*.parquet
*.fst
*.rds

# ---- pipeline run artifacts -------------------------------------------------
Rplots.pdf
*.log

# ---- renv: keep renv.lock, activate.R, settings.json; ignore the library ----
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/cellar/
renv/staging/
renv/sandbox/
renv/python/

# ---- R session artifacts ----------------------------------------------------
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/
# RStudio project file (machine/user specific)
*.Rproj

# ---- OS / editor junk -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
# macOS AppleDouble resource-fork files
._*
Thumbs.db
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---- site-specific config & reference (each site supplies its own) ----------
config/config.yaml
config/hospital_pathway_map.csv

# ---- study documents & single-site outputs (not part of the shared pipeline) -
# The protocol and the OHSU pre-federation report are authored/rendered
# artifacts, not code the pipeline needs; keep them out of the code repository.
clif_hospice_protocol_*.docx
*prefederation_report*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# INTENTIONALLY TRACKED (do NOT ignore) — every site must use the same version
# of the shared reference files for cross-site comparability:
#   reference/crosswalk_ccsr_to_acuity.csv
#   config/network_standard_population.csv
#   reference/hospital_ccn_map.csv
# And the reproducibility anchors:
#   renv.lock          (pinned package versions)
#   .here              (project-root anchor for here::here())
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
